---
description: Keep interface labels, hints, and placeholders short and generic
alwaysApply: true
---

# UI copy

Write labels, hints, placeholders, empty states, and helper lines so they stay short and generic.

- Prefer the label alone. Skip a hint when the label already says what the field is.
- Do not put sample values in fields or placeholders. No client codes, personal names, or example sentences.
- If a hint is necessary, use one short generic line. Do not explain the workflow, name a product behavior, or say what the user can do later.
- Validation messages can name the problem. They should not include an example value.

```text
Bad: placeholder="CBI"
Bad: Short identifier for this library, such as CBI.
Bad: Add each person with the Google address they will use to sign in. You can add more people later.

Good: Client initial
Good: Add a name and email for each person.
```
